      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUNAR MOON (1) was an effortless winner two back when prominent throughout then got further back last time but came home hard into third and beaten one length at this track (17.82). Safe beginner who draws ideally on the inside. Sure to be about the mark. RUN ROLEX (5) boasts a strong record this journey here with three wins and two minors from eight tries. Comes off a (17.66) win last time, scoring by one length in a Grade 5 over 300m at this track. Looks one of the chances. MY JULIA (2) stalked the lead after a clean break from the tricky draw and went on to finish second (17.54) at this track in a Grade 4 over 300m. Expected to feature. TRUE BLUE BILLY (6) is going well, finishing in the placings twice in a row. Not beaten far last time when a 1.5 lengths second (17.81) in a Grade 5 at this track. Solid beginner and with a good start can clear the tricky draw.",
